{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_3>\nimport sys\nfrom math import factorial\n\ndef A(n, k):\n    return factorial(n) // factorial(n - k)\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    mod = int(data[1])\n    \n    if n == 1:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    \n    z = [1]\n    total = 0\n    \n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        new_z = [0] * (i * i // 2)\n        \n        for j in range(len(z)):\n            if z[j]:\n                for k in range(i):\n                    new_z[i - k - 1 + j] += z[j]\n        \n        d = [0] * (len(z) + 1)\n        for w in range(len(z) - 1, -1, -1):\n            d[w] = (d[w + 1] + z[w]) % mod\n        \n        e = [0] * (len(d) + 1)\n        f = [0] * (len(d) + 1)\n        for w in range(len(d)):\n            e[w + 1] = (e[w] + d[w]) % mod\n            f[w + 1] = (f[w] - w * d[w]) % mod\n        \n        current_contribution = 0\n        for jj in range(len(z)):\n            L = jj + 2\n            R = min(len(z) - 1, i + jj)\n            if R >= L:\n                term = ((e[R + 1] - e[L]) * (i + 1 + jj) + (f[R + 1] - f[L])) % mod\n                current_contribution = (current_contribution + term * z[jj]) % mod\n        \n        total = (total + current_contribution * A(n, n - i)) % mod\n        z = new_z\n    \n    print(total % mod)\n\nsolve()\n</your_rewritten_code_3>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static long MOD;\n\n    static long factorial(long n) {\n        long result = 1;\n        for (long i = 2; i <= n; i++) {\n            result = (result * i) % MOD;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    static long modInverse(long a) {\n        return modPow(a, MOD - 2);\n    }\n\n    static long modPow(long base, long exp) {\n        base %= MOD;\n        long result = 1;\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) {\n                result = (result * base) % MOD;\n            }\n            base = (base * base) % MOD;\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    static long A(long n, long k) {\n        long numerator = factorial(n);\n        long denominator = factorial(n - k);\n        return (numerator * modInverse(denominator)) % MOD;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String[] data = br.readLine().split(\" \");\n        long n = Long.parseLong(data[0]);\n        MOD = Long.parseLong(data[1]);\n        \n        if (n == 1) {\n            System.out.println(0);\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        List<Long> z = new ArrayList<>();\n        z.add(1L);\n        long total = 0;\n        \n        for (long i = 2; i <= n; i++) {\n            List<Long> new_z = new ArrayList<>();\n            int new_z_size = (int)(i * i / 2);\n            for (int j = 0; j < new_z_size; j++) {\n                new_z.add(0L);\n            }\n            \n            for (int j = 0; j < z.size(); j++) {\n                if (z.get(j) != 0) {\n                    for (int k = 0; k < i; k++) {\n                        int idx = (int)(i - k - 1 + j);\n                        if (idx < new_z.size()) {\n                            new_z.set(idx, (new_z.get(idx) + z.get(j)) % MOD);\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            \n            List<Long> d = new ArrayList<>();\n            for (int j = 0; j <= z.size(); j++) {\n                d.add(0L);\n            }\n            for (int w = z.size() - 1; w >= 0; w--) {\n                d.set(w, (d.get(w + 1) + z.get(w)) % MOD);\n            }\n            \n            List<Long> e = new ArrayList<>();\n            List<Long> f = new ArrayList<>();\n            for (int j = 0; j <= d.size(); j++) {\n                e.add(0L);\n                f.add(0L);\n            }\n            for (int w = 0; w < d.size(); w++) {\n                e.set(w + 1, (e.get(w) + d.get(w)) % MOD);\n                long temp = (f.get(w) - w * d.get(w)) % MOD;\n                if (temp < 0) temp += MOD;\n                f.set(w + 1, temp);\n            }\n            \n            long current_contribution = 0;\n            for (int jj = 0; jj < z.size(); jj++) {\n                long L = jj + 2;\n                long R = Math.min(z.size() - 1, i + jj);\n                if (R >= L) {\n                    long term = ((e.get((int)(R + 1)) - e.get((int)L) + MOD) % MOD * (i + 1 + jj) % MOD + \n                                (f.get((int)(R + 1)) - f.get((int)L) + MOD) % MOD) % MOD;\n                    current_contribution = (current_contribution + term * z.get(jj)) % MOD;\n                }\n            }\n            \n            total = (total + current_contribution * A(n, n - i)) % MOD;\n            z = new_z;\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println((total % MOD + MOD) % MOD);\n    }\n